  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. The end-growing chain at general L: constants and derivation\n\nReference bra ⟨Ω| = (v ⊗ u)^⊗L with v.u = 0 (identical BPS pairs). Torus-rotated predecessors: **P_k** = ⟨Ω| with the first k sites rotated by the global-torus element γ, i.e. A site v -> vΛ⁻¹, F site u -> uΛ (P_0 = Ω; P_2L = ρ(γ)Ω). Write θ_ks = θ_k − θ_s. The letters of the end-growing chain t₁(θ₁)⁻¹ t₁(θ₂) t₁(θ₃)⁻¹ t₁(θ₄) ⋯ act as\n\n- k odd (A site, inverse letter):  P_k · t₁(θ_k) = (1/d_k) P_{k-1},  i.e. P_{k-1} t₁(θ_k)⁻¹ = d_k P_k;\n- k even (F site, forward letter):  P_{k-1} · t₁(θ_k) = d_k P_k;\n\nwith (ϑ = shifted differences)\n\n  **1/d_k = h ∏_{s≠k} ϑ_ks, ϑ_ks = θ_ks (s an F site), θ_ks + h (s an A site)**  (k odd),\n  **d_k = −h ∏_{s≠k} ϑ̃_ks, ϑ̃_ks = θ_ks (s an A site), θ_ks − h (s an F site)**  (k even).\n\nThe cumulative constants are c_k = d₁ ⋯ d_k (word t₁(θ₁)⁻¹ t₁(θ₂) ⋯ applied to Ω equals c_k P_k). In particular c₁ = d₁ = 1/(h ∏_{F s} θ_1s ∏_{A s≠1}(θ_1s + h)) (the §5.5 formula, now proved for all L), **c₁₂ := c₂ = d₁d₂ = ∏_{A s≥3} θ_2s/(θ_1s + h) · ∏_{F s≥4} (θ_2s − h)/θ_1s**, and for the full chain (global torus) **c_2L = ∏_{F<F'} (h² − θ_FF'²) / ∏_{A<A'} (h² − θ_AA'²)**.\n\n**Proof (all L).** Lemma (one site, BPS contraction). Let a site carry the bra vector w and let a column c (resp. row r) of the auxiliary space be contracted into its Lax operator. For the A-type Lax (x + hK): Σ_j c_j L_ij = x c_i ⟨w| + h w_i ⟨c|, and Σ_i r_i L_ij = x r_j ⟨w| + h (r.w) ⟨j|. For the F-type Lax (x − hP): Σ_j c_j L_ij = x c_i ⟨w| − h (w.c) ⟨i|, and Σ_i r_i L_ij = x r_j ⟨w| − h w_j ⟨r|. So the site acts as the SCALAR x on the aux column/row if the vectors are BPS-orthogonal (A with row, F with column), and as the scalar x + h (A with column, w = c) resp. x − h (F with row, w = r) if the two vectors coincide. - The Lax at u = θ_k is hK_ak (A) or −hP_ak (F), so\n\n- k odd: t₁(θ_k) = h Σ_ij e_ij^(k) [M_> Λ M_<]_ji with M_< = L₁⋯L_{k-1}, M_> = L_{k+1}⋯L_2L; acting on P_k (site k vector v' = vΛ⁻¹) one gets Σ_i [M_<]_li v'_i: every F site to the left carries u' = uΛ with u'.v' = 0 (scalar θ_ks), every A site carries v' = the column (scalar θ_ks + h). Then Λ turns v' into v, and M_> contracted with the column v gives the same pattern with unrotated vectors. Finally Σ_j v_j ⟨j|_k = ⟨v|_k is the UNROTATED site-k vector: P_k t₁(θ_k) = h ∏_{s≠k} ϑ_ks · P_{k-1}.\n- k even: t₁(θ_k) = −h Σ_ab e_ba^(k) [M_> Λ M_<]_ba, ⟨u|e_ba = u_b ⟨a|: the row u is contracted into M_> (A sites: u.v = 0, scalar θ_ks; F sites: same vector, scalar θ_ks − h), Λ turns u into u' = uΛ, and the row u' goes through M_< (A sites v' with u'.v' = 0: θ_ks; F sites: θ_ks − h); the leftover Σ_a u'_a ⟨a|_k = ⟨u'|_k is the ROTATED F vector: P_{k-1} t₁(θ_k) = −h ∏_{s≠k} ϑ̃_ks · P_k.\n\nNo condition on h, θ, z (diagonal), a (W_a) or the pair is used except v.u = 0 and that all pairs carry the SAME (v, u) (for independent pairs the A-A and F-F exchange terms do not collapse; seen in `abjm-nongood-reference-limit.wb`). The singlet terms (r.w) and (w.c) vanish exactly because Λ⁻¹ on A / Λ on F preserves v.u = 0: this is why the fixed rotations are the global-torus γ and nothing else.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* step constants d_k and cumulative constants c_k = d_1 ... d_k ; h optional *)\nobD[k_, th_List, Lp_, hh_: obh] := Module[{ty = obTypes[Lp], n = 2 Lp},\n   If[OddQ[k],\n    1/(hh Product[If[s == k, 1, If[ty[[s]] == \"F\", th[[k]] - th[[s]], th[[k]] - th[[s]] + hh]], {s, n}]),\n    -hh Product[If[s == k, 1, If[ty[[s]] == \"A\", th[[k]] - th[[s]], th[[k]] - th[[s]] - hh]], {s, n}]]];\nobC[k_, th_List, Lp_, hh_: obh] := Product[obD[j, th, Lp, hh], {j, k}];\n(* closed forms quoted in the text *)\nobC1[th_List, Lp_, hh_: obh] := 1/(hh Product[th[[1]] - th[[2 f]], {f, Lp}] Product[th[[1]] - th[[2 a - 1]] + hh, {a, 2, Lp}]);\nobC12[th_List, Lp_, hh_: obh] := Product[(th[[2]] - th[[2 a - 1]])/(th[[1]] - th[[2 a - 1]] + hh), {a, 2, Lp}] Product[(th[[2]] - th[[2 f]] - hh)/(th[[1]] - th[[2 f]]), {f, 2, Lp}];\nobC2L[th_List, Lp_, hh_: obh] := Product[hh^2 - (th[[2 f]] - th[[2 g]])^2, {f, 1, Lp}, {g, f + 1, Lp}]/Product[hh^2 - (th[[2 a - 1]] - th[[2 b - 1]])^2, {a, 1, Lp}, {b, a + 1, Lp}];\n(* symbolic check of the three closed forms for L = 1..4 pairs (symbolic theta_s, symbolic h): difference = 0 after Together *)\nobSymChecks = Table[Module[{th = Array[obq, 2 Lp]},\n    {Lp, Together[obC[1, th, Lp, obhs] - obC1[th, Lp, obhs]] === 0, Together[obC[2, th, Lp, obhs] - obC12[th, Lp, obhs]] === 0, Together[obC[2 Lp, th, Lp, obhs] - obC2L[th, Lp, obhs]] === 0}], {Lp, 1, 4}];\nobTH = {2/7, -3/5, 8/11, -11/8, 5/13, -7/9, 4/15, -9/11}; obZ = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3, 4/7};\nobStdL2 = {obC[1, obTH[[;; 4]], 2], obC[2, obTH[[;; 4]], 2], obC[3, obTH[[;; 4]], 2], obC[4, obTH[[;; 4]], 2]};\nGrid[Join[{{\"L (pairs)\", \"c1 = closed form\", \"c12 = c2 = closed form\", \"c_2L = pair product\"}}, obSymChecks, {{}, {\"L = 2 standard point\", \"c1, c2, c3, c4 =\", obStdL2, \"\"}, {\"quoted (task)\", \"c1 = 603680/25947, c3 = -321399232/112262625, c4 = -1108723/174000\", obStdL2[[1]] == 603680/25947 && obStdL2[[3]] == -321399232/112262625 && obStdL2[[4]] == -1108723/174000, \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"725119\" data-output-id=\"237\" data-out-n=\"123\" data-sub-idx=\"11\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"4\" data-sub-start=\"15\" data-sub-end=\"15\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[123]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"17\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:9.65em;vertical-align:-4.555em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.095em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.055em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.055em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:9.61em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-4.555em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.055em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.215em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">L (pairs)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.015em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.815em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.615em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span><span st