  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Three independent exact parameter sets at L = 2 and L = 3 (the closed forms are a derived statement, so these are validations, not fits): P1 the standard point with W_a (a = 1/3); P2 other theta, z and a = -2/5; P3 other theta, z, **h = 3/7** and a generic integer BPS pair v = (2,-1,3,1), u = (1,2,1,-3) (v.u = 0, not of the W_a form). For each: all d_k agree exactly, every residual vector is exactly 0, and the product of all 2L constants equals the pair-product formula c_2L.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "obPoints = {\n   <|\"name\" -> \"P1: standard, W_a (a=1/3)\", \"th\" -> obTH, \"z\" -> obZ, \"ref\" -> (obRefW[#, 1/3] &), \"h\" -> 1/2|>,\n   <|\"name\" -> \"P2: other th, z; W_a (a=-2/5)\", \"th\" -> {3/5, -1/4, 7/9, -5/6, 2/3, -3/7, 1/3, -4/5}, \"z\" -> {7/5, 3/4, 9/8, 5/6}, \"ref\" -> (obRefW[#, -2/5] &), \"h\" -> 1/2|>,\n   <|\"name\" -> \"P3: other th, z, h = 3/7; generic BPS pair\", \"th\" -> {-1/3, 5/6, 1/9, -7/4, 3/8, 11/10, -2/5, 1/7}, \"z\" -> {2, 1/2, 5/3, 3/10}, \"ref\" -> (Flatten[Table[{{2, -1, 3, 1}, {1, 2, 1, -3}}, #], 1] &), \"h\" -> 3/7|>};\nobPointRows = Flatten[Table[Module[{res, th = pt[\"th\"][[;; 2 Lp]], hh = pt[\"h\"]}, obSetup[Lp];\n     res = obStepCheck[Lp, th, pt[\"z\"], pt[\"ref\"][Lp], hh];\n     {pt[\"name\"], Lp, AllTrue[res[[All, 5]], # === 0 &], AllTrue[res[[All, 6]], # === \"exactly 0\" &], res[[1, 3]] == obC1[th, Lp, hh], Times @@ res[[1 ;; 2, 3]] == obC12[th, Lp, hh], Times @@ res[[All, 3]] == obC2L[th, Lp, hh]}], {pt, obPoints}, {Lp, 2, 3}], 1];\nGrid[Prepend[obPointRows, {\"parameter set\", \"L (pairs)\", \"all d_k = closed form\", \"all residual vectors exactly 0\", \"c1 = closed form\", \"c12 = closed form\", \"c_2L = pair-product formula\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
