  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. The one-field bridge families at L = 3 pairs (6 sites)\n\n**Families.** From section 1, with pair p = ⌈k/2⌉ and parameters (c, a, φ) (z = 1 + εφ, θ = θ_ABJM + δθ⁰, θ_ABJM = (1,0,1,0,1,0), θ⁰ = standard point, δ = ε):\n\n- **F-site family (a)** (k = 2p even): ⟨W_a^L| t₁(θ₁)⁻¹ t₁(θ₂) ⋯ t₁(θ_{k-1})⁻¹ (α + β t₁(θ_k)) = ⟨W_a^L| ρ_{1..k-1}(γ) ρ_k(α c_{k-1} + β c_k Λ); choosing α = (cε − 1)/c_{k-1}, β = 1/c_k puts **u(cε − 1 + Λ)** = ε [(c+φ₄) e₄ − a(c+φ₁) e₁] on the F site of pair p: pair p -> (e₁ + a (z₁/z₄) e₄)⊗(e₄ − a' e₁), a' = a(c+φ₁)/(c+φ₄); normalised T_ε := bra_ε/(ε(c+φ₄)) -> N_ε -> B* (pair p = (e₁ + a e₄)⊗(e₄ − a' e₁), all other pairs W_a).\n- **A-site family (b)** (k = 2p − 1 odd): ⟨W_a^L| … (α + β t₁(θ_k)⁻¹) = ⟨W_a^L|ρ_{1..k-1}(γ)ρ_k(α c_{k-1} + β c_k Λ⁻¹); α = 1/c_{k-1}, β = −κ/c_k, κ = 1 − cε puts **v(1 − κΛ⁻¹)** = ε (c+φ₁)/z₁ (e₁ + a'' e₄) on the A site, a'' = a (c+φ₄) z₁/((c+φ₁) z₄); T_ε := bra_ε/(ε(c+φ₁)).\n- **Chain of fixed letters.** In both families the fixed rotations on the sites before k are the torus γ (Λ⁻¹ on A, Λ on F), which tend to 1 as z -> 1: the limit bra has W_a on all pairs except pair p.\n\n**Finite-twist identity.** For a twisted eigenstate Ψ_ε of t₁, ⟨bra_ε|Ψ_ε⟩ = (word eigenvalue) · ⟨W_a^L|Ψ_ε⟩, e.g. [(α + βτ(θ_k)) ∏_{j<k} τ(θ_j)^{(−)^j}] ⟨W|Ψ⟩ for F; both sides are computed independently (left: product bra; right: eigenvalues read off Ψ_ε with the transfer matrices).\n\n**Limit (HW trick).** For an untwisted highest-weight Ψ₀ the global upper unitriangular rotation ρ(n), n = exp(−a E₁₄), is trivial. It maps W_a -> vac (A: e₁ + a e₄ -> e₁; F: e₄ − a e₁ -> e₄) and pair p of B* -> e₁ ⊗ (e₄ + (a − a') e₁): **⟨B*|Ψ₀⟩ = ⟨vac^L|Ψ₀⟩ + (a − a') ⟨e₁e₁ (pair p) vac^{L-1}|Ψ₀⟩**; for (b): ⟨vac^L|Ψ₀⟩ + (a'' − a)⟨e₄e₄ (pair p) vac^{L-1}|Ψ₀⟩ with a'' = a(c+φ₄)/(c+φ₁). For the weight (L−1)(ε₁ − ε₄) states the second terms are the bridge-ℓ = 1 structure constant C₁ of the project bra B₁ = e₁ ⊗ (e₄ + e₁) ⊗ W₋₁^{L-1}.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* exact rational test at a finite-twist ABJM-type point, L = 3: theta = theta_ABJM + delta theta0, z = 1 + eps phi, delta = eps = 1/10 *)\nobBraSV[Lp_, a_, z_List, k_, cc_, eps_] := Module[{sv = obRefW[Lp, a], I4 = IdentityMatrix[4]},\n   Do[sv = obRot[sv, j, If[OddQ[j], DiagonalMatrix[1/z], DiagonalMatrix[z]]], {j, k - 1}];\n   If[EvenQ[k], obRot[sv, k, (cc eps - 1) I4 + DiagonalMatrix[z]], obRot[sv, k, I4 - (1 - cc eps) DiagonalMatrix[1/z]]]];\nobAlphaBeta[Lp_, k_, cc_, eps_, th_] := If[EvenQ[k], {(cc eps - 1)/obC[k - 1, th, Lp], 1/obC[k, th, Lp]}, {1/obC[k - 1, th, Lp], -(1 - cc eps)/obC[k, th, Lp]}];\n(* inverse-free word identity:  bra . prod_{odd j <= k}(t(th_j)) = Wb . prod_{even j < k} t(th_j) . (alpha + beta t(th_k)) [k even]  or (alpha t(th_k) + beta) [k odd] *)\nobWordResidual[Lp_, k_, a_, z_List, th_List, cc_, eps_] := Module[{bp, Wb, al, be, T, lhs, rhs},\n   bp = obProd[obBraSV[Lp, a, z, k, cc, eps]]; Wb = obProd[obRefW[Lp, a]];\n   {al, be} = obAlphaBeta[Lp, k, cc, eps, th];\n   T[x_, j_] := obApplyT[x, th, z, th[[j]]];\n   If[EvenQ[k],\n    lhs = Fold[T, bp, Range[1, k - 1, 2]]; rhs = Fold[T, Wb, Range[2, k - 2, 2]]; rhs = al rhs + be T[rhs, k],\n    lhs = Fold[T, bp, Range[1, k, 2]]; rhs = Fold[T, Wb, Range[2, k - 1, 2]]; rhs = al T[rhs, k] + be rhs];\n   Flatten[lhs - rhs]];\nobThABJM = {1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0};\nobPhi1 = {9/10, 2/5, -3/10, -11/10}; obPhi2 = {13/10, -1/5, 1/2, -7/10};\nobSetup[3];\nobEx = Table[Module[{eps = 1/10, th, z, res},\n    th = obThABJM + eps obTH[[;; 6]]; z = 1 + eps obPhi1;\n    res = obWordResidual[3, k, 1/3, z, th, 2, eps];\n    {k, If[EvenQ[k], \"F-site family (a)\", \"A-site family (b)\"], Ceiling[k/2], AllTrue[res, # === 0 &], Length[res]}], {k, 1, 6}];\nGrid[Prepend[obEx, {\"k\", \"family\", \"pair p\", \"residual vector exactly 0 (exact rational arithmetic)\", \"vector length\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
