  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**[numpy cross-check of the cell above; the Wolfram cell was NOT run, see the status note at the end]** Pair-1 families, phi1 = (0.9, 0.4, -0.3, -1.1), c = 2, a = 1/3, theta = theta_ABJM + eps theta0, z = 1 + eps phi1. T_eps -> limit with rate 1 (error 9e-3, 9e-4, 9e-5 for the vacuum; 4.6e-3, 4.65e-4, 4.66e-5 for the E = 8 states, F family; 1.5e-3, 1.5e-4, 1.5e-5, A family), the finite-twist identity |LHS_prod - RHS_tau| <= 5.6e-15 at every row, |<Psi0|Psi_eps>| >= 0.9999:\n\n| family | state (Dynkin, E_MZ) | eps | |<Psi0|Psi_eps>| | <W_a^3|Psi_eps> | T_eps | limit | |T - limit| | identity residual |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F (a), k=2 | [3,0,3], 0 | 1e-2 | 1.000000 | 1 | 0.99108 | 1 | 8.92e-03 | 1.9e-16 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [3,0,3], 0 | 1e-3 | 1.000000 | 1 | 0.9991 | 1 | 8.99e-04 | 1.5e-16 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [3,0,3], 0 | 1e-4 | 1.000000 | 1 | 0.99991 | 1 | 9.00e-05 | 1.9e-17 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [2,0,2], 8 | 1e-2 | 0.999926 | -0.00069-0.00067i | -0.003408-0.1481i | -0.1512i | 4.62e-03 | 3.0e-15 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [2,0,2], 8 | 1e-3 | 0.999999 | -6.81e-05-6.79e-05i | -0.0003456-0.1509i | -0.1512i | 4.65e-04 | 2.8e-15 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [2,0,2], 8 | 1e-4 | 1.000000 | -6.805e-06-6.803e-06i | -3.461e-05-0.1512i | -0.1512i | 4.66e-05 | 3.3e-15 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [2,0,2], 16 | 1e-2 | 0.999907 | -0.00067 | -0.14782 | -0.1512 | 3.38e-03 | 2.9e-15 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [2,0,2], 16 | 1e-3 | 0.999999 | -6.80e-05 | -0.15086 | -0.1512 | 3.40e-04 | 2.0e-15 |\n| F (a), k=2 | [2,0,2], 16 | 1e-4 | 1.000000 | -6.80e-06 | -0.15117 | -0.1512 | 3.40e-05 | 3.5e-15 |\n| A (b), k=1 | [3,0,3], 0 | 1e-2 / 1e-3 / 1e-4 | 1.000000 | 1 | 0.99108 / 0.9991 / 0.99991 | 1 | 8.9e-3 / 9.0e-4 / 9.0e-5 | 3.3e-16 |\n| A (b), k=1 | [2,0,2], 8 | 1e-2 | 0.999926 | -0.00069-0.00067i | -0.001242-0.04614i | -0.046925i | 1.47e-03 | 3.0e-15 |\n| A (b), k=1 | [2,0,2], 8 | 1e-3 | 0.999999 | -6.81e-05-6.79e-05i | -0.0001257-0.04685i | -0.046925i | 1.48e-04 | 2.8e-15 |\n| A (b), k=1 | [2,0,2], 8 | 1e-4 | 1.000000 | -6.805e-06-6.803e-06i | -1.258e-05-0.04692i | -0.046925i | 1.48e-05 | 3.3e-15 |\n| A (b), k=1 | [2,0,2], 16 | 1e-2 | 0.999907 | -0.00067 | -0.04593 | -0.046925 | 9.95e-04 | 3.0e-15 |\n| A (b), k=1 | [2,0,2], 16 | 1e-3 | 0.999999 | -6.80e-05 | -0.046825 | -0.046925 | 1.00e-04 | 1.9e-15 |\n| A (b), k=1 | [2,0,2], 16 | 1e-4 | 1.000000 | -6.80e-06 | -0.046915 | -0.046925 | 1.00e-05 | 3.5e-15 |\n\nThe partner state E = 8 with C_1 = -i/sqrt(24) gives the complex-conjugate rows. Controls: the states #2 [4,0,0] and #3 [1,2,1] (weights (3,-1,-1,-1), (2,1,-1,-2)) have T_eps = 0 and limit 0 identically (the product bras only have weights (x,0,0,-x)). The remaining states (#4 and #8-#26, weight sectors of dimension up to 256) were run in numpy only: T_eps -> 0 as eps -> 0, namely identically 0 for #4 and #8-#16 (weights (2,1,-1,-2), (2,0,-1,-1), (1,1,1,-3), (1,1,0,-2), (1,1,-1,-1)) and O(eps^2) or O(eps) for the [1,0,1] and [0,0,0] states #17-#26 (e.g. 3.1e-6, 3.1e-8, 3.1e-10 for E = 10.34, F family), identity residual <= 4e-15 throughout. Limit values: F: (a - a') C_1 = -0.7407 C_1; A: (a'' - a) C_1 = -0.22989 C_1; C_1 = i/sqrt(24), -i/sqrt(24), 1/sqrt(24) for E_MZ = 8, 8, 16.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 2c. phi- and c-independence, convergence rates, control against the project bra B_1\n\nThe limit depends on (phi, c) only through a' = a(c+phi_1)/(c+phi_4) (F) resp. a'' = a(c+phi_4)/(c+phi_1) (A); the estimator X_est = (T_eps - V0)/(a - a') (F) or (T_eps - V0)/(a'' - a) (A) must tend to X = C_1 (data file) for every (phi, c). Three cases: (phi1, c = 2), (phi2 = (1.3,-0.2,0.5,-0.7), c = 2), (phi1, c = 0.5). Then the convergence rates log10(err(eps)/err(eps/10)) (1 = O(eps)) and the special point a = -1, c = -phi_4 (kappa = z_4) of family (b), where the bra is exactly (1 - z_4/z_1) B_1 and z_1 T_eps = <B_1|Psi_eps> for every eps (section 5.5 / 5.7 formula).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "obCases = {{\"phi1, c=2\", \"phi1\", obPhi1f, 2.}, {\"phi2, c=2\", \"phi2\", obPhi2f, 2.}, {\"phi1, c=0.5\", \"phi1\", obPhi1f, 0.5}};\nobA2 = Table[Table[Table[Table[Module[{tw = obGetTw[cs[[2]], cs[[3]], eps, eps]}, obRow[i, tw[i], k, 1/3, cs[[4]], cs[[3]], eps, eps]], {i, {5, 6, 7}}], {eps, {0.001, 0.0001}}], {k, {2, 1}}], {cs, obCases}];\nobXest[r_, cs_] := With[{a = 1/3, c = cs[[4]], phi = cs[[3]]}, (r[\"T\"] - obV0[[r[\"i\"]]])/If[EvenQ[r[\"k\"]], a - a (c + phi[[1]])/(c + phi[[4]]), a (c + phi[[4]])/(c + phi[[1]]) - a]];\nobA2rows = Flatten[Table[With[{r = obA2[[ci, ki, ei, si]], cs = obCases[[ci]]},\n     {cs[[1]], If[ki == 1, \"F (a), k=2\", \"A (b), k=1\"], r[\"eps\"], r[\"i\"], N[obHW[[r[\"i\"], \"E\"]]], obFmt[r[\"T\"]], obFmt[obXest[r, cs]], obFmt[obHW[[r[\"i\"], \"C\"]][[2]]], obFmt[Abs[obXest[r, cs] - obHW[[r[\"i\"], \"C\"]][[2]]]]}], {ci, 3}, {ki, 2}, {ei, 2}, {si, 3}], 3];\nobRates = Flatten[Table[{If[ki == 1, \"F (a), k=2\", \"A (b), k=1\"], obHW[[obStates[[si]], \"dyn\"]], N[obHW[[obStates[[si]], \"E\"]]], N[Log10[obA1[[ki, 1, si]][\"err\"]/obA1[[ki, 2, si]][\"err\"]], 3], N[Log10[obA1[[ki, 2, si]][\"err\"]/obA1[[ki, 3, si]][\"err\"]], 3]}, {ki, 2}, {si, 4}], 1];\nobB1 = obProd[Join[{obE[1], obE[4] + obE[1]}, Flatten[Table[{obE[1] - obE[4], obE[4] + obE[1]}, 2], 1]]];\nobB1rows = Flatten[Table[Module[{z = 1. + eps obPhi1f, tw = obGetTw[\"phi1\", obPhi1f, eps, eps], r},\n     r = obRow[i, tw[i], 1, -1., -obPhi1f[[4]], obPhi1f, eps, eps];\n     {obHW[[i, \"dyn\"]], eps, obFmt[z[[1]] r[\"T\"]], obFmt[obB1 . tw[i][\"psi\"]], obFmt[Abs[z[[1]] r[\"T\"] - obB1 . tw[i][\"psi\"]]], obFmt[obHW[[i, \"C\"]][[2]]]}], {i, {1, 5, 6, 7}}, {eps, obEpsList}], 1];\nColumn[{Grid[Prepend[obA2rows, {\"(phi, c)\", \"family\", \"eps\", \"state #\", \"E_MZ\", \"T_eps\", \"X_est\", \"C_1 (data)\", \"|X_est - C_1|\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[obRates, {\"family\", \"Dynkin\", \"E_MZ\", \"rate 1e-2 -> 1e-3\", \"rate 1e-3 -> 1e-4\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[obB1rows, {\"Dynkin\", \"eps\", \"z1 T_eps (a=-1, kappa=z4)\", \"<B_1|Psi_eps>\", \"difference\", \"C_1 (data)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"725119\" data-output-id=\"242\" data-out-n=\"178\" data-sub-idx=\"7\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"21\" data-sub-start=\"10\" data-sub-end=\"12\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[178]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div data-wolfram-is-skeleton=\"1\" data-wolfram-atom-count=\"1149\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"17\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:71.23em;vertical-align:-35.365em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:35.865em;\"><span style=\"top:-37.865em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:24.615em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:22.615em;\"><span style=\"top:-24.575em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:24.575em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:44.65em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-22.075em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:22.575em;\"><span style=\"top:-24.735em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(phi, c)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-23.525em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span