   "value": "**[numpy cross-check of the cell above; the Wolfram cell was NOT run, see the status note at the end]**\n\nphi- and c-independence at eps = 1e-4. The three cases have different a' (F family) and a'' (A family): (phi1, c=2): a' = 1.07407, a'' = 0.10345; (phi2, c=2): a' = 0.84615, a'' = 0.13131; (phi1, c=0.5): a' = -0.77778, a'' = -0.14286, so the limits of T_eps themselves differ (e.g. -0.1512, -0.1047, +0.2268 times i for the E = 8 state, F family), but the estimator X_est = (T - V0)/(a - a') (F) resp. (T - V0)/(a'' - a) (A) is universal and equals C_1 of the data file up to the O(eps) error:\n\n| (phi, c) | family | state | T_eps | X_est | C_1 (data) | abs. difference |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| phi1, c=2 | F (a), k=2 | #5 (E=8) | -3.461e-05-0.1512i | 4.673e-05+0.2041i | 0.20412i | 6.3e-05 |\n| phi1, c=2 | F (a), k=2 | #7 (E=16) | -0.15117 | 0.20408 | 0.20412 | 4.6e-05 |\n| phi1, c=2 | A (b), k=1 | #5 | -1.258e-05-0.04692i | 5.472e-05+0.2041i | 0.20412i | 6.4e-05 |\n| phi1, c=2 | A (b), k=1 | #7 | -0.046915 | 0.20408 | 0.20412 | 4.4e-05 |\n| phi2, c=2 | F (a), k=2 | #5 | -2.605e-05-0.1047i | 5.08e-05+0.2041i | 0.20412i | 7.4e-05 |\n| phi2, c=2 | F (a), k=2 | #7 | -0.10465 | 0.20407 | 0.20412 | 5.7e-05 |\n| phi2, c=2 | A (b), k=1 | #5 | -1.188e-05-0.04123i | 5.88e-05+0.2041i | 0.20412i | 7.4e-05 |\n| phi2, c=2 | A (b), k=1 | #7 | -0.041226 | 0.20407 | 0.20412 | 5.5e-05 |\n| phi1, c=0.5 | F (a), k=2 | #5 | 3.491e-05+0.2268i | 3.142e-05+0.2041i | 0.20412i | 4.1e-05 |\n| phi1, c=0.5 | F (a), k=2 | #7 | 0.22677 | 0.20409 | 0.20412 | 3.1e-05 |\n| phi1, c=0.5 | A (b), k=1 | #5 | -1.877e-05-0.09719i | 3.942e-05+0.2041i | 0.20412i | 4.4e-05 |\n| phi1, c=0.5 | A (b), k=1 | #7 | -0.097189 | 0.2041 | 0.20412 | 2.8e-05 |\n\n(State #6 = complex conjugate of #5.) Convergence rates log10(err(eps)/err(eps/10)), pair 1 (from the 2b table): F family: vacuum 0.996/1.000, E=8 states 0.997/1.000, E=16 0.998/1.000; A family: vacuum 0.996/1.000, E=8 states 0.997/1.000, E=16 0.998/1.000 (columns 1e-2 -> 1e-3 and 1e-3 -> 1e-4): rate 1 = O(eps) everywhere.\n\nB_1 control, A family at a = -1, c = -phi_4 (kappa = z_4): the bra is exactly (1 - z_4/z_1) B_1 and z_1 T_eps = <B_1|Psi_eps> for every eps (difference <= 1.1e-13), the limit being the data value C_1 = 1 (vacuum), +-0.204124 i (E = 8), 0.204124 (E = 16):\n\n| state | eps | z_1 T_eps | <B_1|Psi_eps> | difference |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [3,0,3] | 1e-2 / 1e-3 / 1e-4 | 1 / 1 / 1 | 1 / 1 / 1 | 7e-15 / 3e-14 / 2e-14 |\n| [2,0,2] E=8 | 1e-2 | 0.004547+0.2034i | 0.004547+0.2034i | 1.5e-15 |\n| [2,0,2] E=8 | 1e-3 | 0.0004554+0.2041i | 0.0004554+0.2041i | 6.3e-15 |\n| [2,0,2] E=8 | 1e-4 | 4.554e-05+0.2041i | 4.554e-05+0.2041i | 1.1e-13 |\n| [2,0,2] E=16 | 1e-2 / 1e-3 / 1e-4 | 0.20251 / 0.20396 / 0.20411 | same | 1.5e-15 / 6e-15 / 1.1e-13 |",
   "languageId": "markdown",
