   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**[numpy cross-check of the cell above; the Wolfram cell was NOT run, see the status note at the end]** Mixed placements, phi1, c = 2, a = 1/3 (the pair-1 rows k = 1, 2 are in the table of section 2b). All six placements converge with rate 1.00 (O(eps)) to the SAME limits as pair 1, namely V0 + (a - a') C_1 = -0.151203 (E = 16 state; -0.151203 i for the E = 8 state) for the F family and V0+ (a'' - a) C_1 = -0.046925 (E = 16; -0.046925 i for E = 8) for the A family, and the finite-twist identity |LHS_prod - RHS_tau| <= 4e-15 holds for every k:\n\n| k (pair) | family | state (E_MZ) | eps | T_eps | limit | |T - limit| | identity residual |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 (2) | A (b) | [3,0,3] (0) | 1e-4 | 0.99971 | 1 | 2.90e-04 | 7.2e-17 |\n| 3 (2) | A (b) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-3 | -8.426e-05-0.04685i | -0.046925i | 1.12e-04 | 2.8e-15 |\n| 3 (2) | A (b) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-4 | -8.437e-06-0.04692i | -0.046925i | 1.12e-05 | 3.3e-15 |\n| 3 (2) | A (b) | [2,0,2] (16) | 1e-4 | -0.046922 | -0.046925 | 2.82e-06 | 3.5e-15 |\n| 4 (2) | F (a) | [3,0,3] (0) | 1e-4 | 0.99971 | 1 | 2.90e-04 | 1.7e-16 |\n| 4 (2) | F (a) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-3 | -0.0001116-0.1508i | -0.1512i | 4.12e-04 | 2.8e-15 |\n| 4 (2) | F (a) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-4 | -1.118e-05-0.1512i | -0.1512i | 4.13e-05 | 3.3e-15 |\n| 4 (2) | F (a) | [2,0,2] (16) | 1e-4 | -0.15117 | -0.1512 | 3.10e-05 | 3.5e-15 |\n| 5 (3) | A (b) | [3,0,3] (0) | 1e-4 | 0.99951 | 1 | 4.90e-04 | 1.0e-16 |\n| 5 (3) | A (b) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-3 | -0.0001161-0.04672i | -0.046925i | 2.35e-04 | 2.8e-15 |\n| 5 (3) | A (b) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-4 | -1.165e-05-0.0469i | -0.046925i | 2.36e-05 | 3.3e-15 |\n| 5 (3) | A (b) | [2,0,2] (16) | 1e-4 | -0.046902 | -0.046925 | 2.29e-05 | 3.5e-15 |\n| 6 (3) | F (a) | [3,0,3] (0) | 1e-4 | 0.99951 | 1 | 4.90e-04 | 2.5e-18 |\n| 6 (3) | F (a) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-3 | -0.0002911-0.1505i | -0.1512i | 7.98e-04 | 2.8e-15 |\n| 6 (3) | F (a) | [2,0,2] (8) | 1e-4 | -2.923e-05-0.1511i | -0.1512i | 7.99e-05 | 3.3e-15 |\n| 6 (3) | F (a) | [2,0,2] (16) | 1e-4 | -0.15112 | -0.1512 | 8.02e-05 | 3.5e-15 |\n\n(The conjugate E = 8 state gives the complex-conjugate values; the controls [4,0,0], [1,2,1] give T = 0 identically.) Rates log10(err(eps)/err(eps/10)), columns 1e-2 -> 1e-3 / 1e-3 -> 1e-4: k = 3: vacuum 0.994/0.999, E=8 0.999/1.000, E=16 1.012/1.001; k = 4: 0.994/0.999, 0.998/1.000, 0.997/1.000; k = 5: 0.990/0.999, 0.992/0.999, 0.992/0.999; k = 6: 0.990/0.999, 0.991/0.999, 0.991/0.999. Cyclicity: the limits of the pair-2 and pair-3 words are those of pair 1 because X11_p = X44_p = C_1 for p = 1, 2, 3 (section 2a table; |psi - S psi| <= 7e-16 for the saved states); at finite eps the words differ from the pair-1 ones only by O(eps) (the torus factors on the earlier sites are not yet 1).",
