  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Homogeneous limit delta -> 0 and the normalised form of the formula\n\n**What is singular and what is not.** At the ABJM point (theta_A - theta_F = 2h) every constant of section 1 is finite and non-zero in the homogeneous limit delta -> 0 (theta pair-periodic): d_k contains only theta_ks with s on the opposite sublattice (= +-2h at delta = 0) or on the same sublattice shifted by +-h (= +-h). In closed form at delta = 0: c_1 = (2 h^2)^(-L) (= 2^L at h = 1/2; c_1 = 8 at L = 3) and d_2 = -h (-2h)^L (-h)^(L-1) (= 1/8 at L = 3), so c_12 = c_1 d_2 = 1. The singular locus is theta_A = theta_F (theta = 0, the 'wrong' chain of the note's 5.7 box): there d_k (k odd) -> infinity like (theta_A - theta_F)^(-L), d_k (k even) -> 0 like (theta_A - theta_F)^L, and the transfer-matrix eigenvalues tau(theta_k) go to zero at the same rate; only the products d_k^(+-1) tau(theta_k) stay finite (checked on the twisted vacuum, whose eigenvalues are known exactly, in the last cell).\n\n**Normalised letters (the analogue of 2603's properly normalised t-hat).** hat t_k := d_k t1(theta_k) for k odd, hat t_k := t1(theta_k)/d_k for k even. Then the localisation identities read P_{k-1} hat t_k^((-1)^k) = P_k with NO constant, the words are\n\n  W_F(p) = [prod_{j<k} hat t_j^((-1)^j)] (c eps - 1 + hat t_k),  k = 2p;   W_A(p) = [prod_{j<k} hat t_j^((-1)^j)] (1 - kappa hat t_k^(-1)),  k = 2p - 1,\n\nacting on the reference as <Omega| W = bra_eps (all bras O(1) up to the explicit factor eps (c + phi_x)), and the finite-twist overlap is **<bra_eps|Psi_eps> = [prod_{j<k} hat tau_j^((-1)^j)] (c eps - 1 + hat tau_k) <W_a^L|Psi_eps>** (F; for A replace the last factor by 1 - kappa/hat tau_k), with hat tau_j = d_j^(+-1) tau(theta_j) the eigenvalue of hat t_j. The vacuum bra is an exact eigenbra with hat tau_j = z_1 (j odd), z_4 (j even) at every theta (last cell). For the one-field F bridge on pair 1 (same form at every L):\n\n  **V0 + (a - a') C_1 = lim_{eps->0} (c eps - 1 + hat tau_2)/(hat tau_1 eps (c + phi_4)) <W_a^L|Psi_eps>**,  a' = a(c+phi_1)/(c+phi_4);\n\nfor the states with V0 = 0 (weight (L-1)(e1 - e4)) one finds numerically hat tau_1 = hat tau_2 in the limit (a fourth root of unity: +i, -i, -1 for the three [2,0,2] states at L = 3) and therefore **C_1 = (1 - 1/hat tau_1) K,  K = lim <W_a^L|Psi_eps>/(eps a (phi_4 - phi_1))**, independent of phi, c and a (tested below at delta = 0). The cells below: (i) delta-scan of T_eps at fixed eps (delta = 0 included), (ii) hat tau and the c-free formula at delta = 0 exactly, (iii) the vacuum eigenvalues and the theta_A -> theta_F behaviour.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "obDeltas = {0.1, 0.01, 0.001, 0.0001, 10.^-6, 0.};\nobScan = Flatten[Table[Module[{eps = 0.001, th = N[obThABJM + dl obTH[[;; 6]]], tw = obGetTw[\"phi1\", obPhi1f, 0.001, dl]},\n     Table[Module[{r = obRow[i, tw[i], 2, 1/3, 2., obPhi1f, 0.001, dl], tau = tw[i][\"taus\"]},\n       {dl, obHW[[i, \"dyn\"]], N[obC[1, th, 3]], N[obD[2, th, 3]], obFmt[tw[i][\"ov\"]], obFmt[obC[1, th, 3] tau[[1]]], obFmt[tau[[2]]/obD[2, th, 3]], obFmt[r[\"T\"]], obFmt[r[\"lim\"]], obFmt[r[\"err\"]]}], {i, {1, 5, 6, 7}}]], {dl, obDeltas}], 1];\nGrid[Prepend[obScan, {\"delta\", \"Dynkin\", \"c1\", \"d2\", \"|<Psi0|Psi_eps>|\", \"hat tau_1\", \"hat tau_2\", \"T_eps (F, pair 1, eps = 1e-3)\", \"limit\", \"|T - limit|\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
