   "value": "**[numpy cross-check of the cell above; the Wolfram cell was NOT run]** Exactly homogeneous twisted chain (delta = 0), F-site family on pair 1, [2,0,2] states (the two E = 8 states are complex conjugates, C_1 = +-i/sqrt(24); E = 16: C_1 = 1/sqrt(24) = 0.204124). Normalised eigenvalues hat tau_1 = hat tau_2 -> i, -i, -1 (fourth roots of unity), K = <W_a^3|Psi_eps>/(eps a (phi_4 - phi_1)) -> (1 + i)/sqrt(96) etc. independent of phi, and (1 - 1/hat tau_1) K -> C_1; rows at eps = 1e-4 and 1e-5 (eps = 1e-3 has the same pattern with 1e-4 accuracy):\n\n| phi | eps | state (E) | hat tau_1 | hat tau_2 | K | (1 - 1/hat tau_1) K | (hat tau_2 - 1) K/hat tau_1 | C_1 (data) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| phi1 | 1e-4 | [2,0,2] (8) | 1.0001i | 0.99993i | 0.10206+0.10206i | 5.78e-6+0.20412i | -7.82e-6+0.20411i | 0.204124i |\n| phi1 | 1e-4 | [2,0,2] (16) | -1.00006 | -0.999927 | 0.10206 | 0.20412 | 0.20411 | 0.204124 |\n| phi1 | 1e-5 | [2,0,2] (8) | 1.00001i | 0.99999i | 0.10206+0.10206i | 5.78e-7+0.20412i | -7.83e-7+0.20412i | 0.204124i |\n| phi1 | 1e-5 | [2,0,2] (16) | -1.00001 | -0.999993 | 0.10206 | 0.20412 | 0.20412 | 0.204124 |\n| phi2 = (1.3,-0.2,0.5,-0.7) | 1e-4 | [2,0,2] (8) | 1.00009i | 0.99996i | 0.10206+0.10206i | 9.86e-6+0.20411i | -3.74e-6+0.20409i | 0.204124i |\n| phi2 | 1e-5 | [2,0,2] (8) | 1.00001i | 1.00000i | 0.10206+0.10206i | 9.87e-7+0.20412i | -3.74e-7+0.20412i | 0.204124i |\n| phi2 | 1e-5 | [2,0,2] (16) | -1.00001 | -0.999996 | 0.10206 | 0.20412 | 0.20412 | 0.204124 |\n| phi3 = (0.5,0.1,-0.4,-1.3) | 1e-4 | [2,0,2] (8) | 1.00003i | 0.99991i | 0.10207+0.10207i | 2.04e-6+0.20413i | -1.02e-5+0.20412i | 0.204124i |\n| phi3 | 1e-5 | [2,0,2] (16) | -1.000003 | -0.999991 | 0.10206 | 0.20412 | 0.20412 | 0.204124 |\n\nSo C_1 = (1 - 1/hat tau_1) K with K the same for all (phi, a, c): K carries the whole eps-dependence of the overlap with the reference, hat tau_1 is the transfer-matrix datum. For the vacuum (V0 = 1) hat tau_1 = z_1 = 1 + eps phi_1 exactly, so the c-dependent form of the formula is needed there (limit 1 comes from (c eps - 1 + hat tau_2)/(hat tau_1 eps (c + phi_4)) -> (c + phi_4)/(c + phi_4)).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* twisted vacuum bra: exact eigenbra of t1; normalised eigenvalues hat tau_j = z_1 (j odd), z_4 (j even) at every theta; and the theta_A -> theta_F behaviour (L = 2, homogeneous theta_A = 0.3, theta_F = 0.3 - d, machine precision) *)\nobSetup[2];\nobVacTest = Table[Module[{z = {1.3, 0.8, 1.1, 0.7}, vac = obProd[Flatten[Table[{obE[1], obE[4]}, 2], 1]], th = {0.3, 0.3 - d, 0.3, 0.3 - d}, y, lam},\n    Table[y = obApplyT[vac, th, z, th[[k]]]; lam = (y . vac)/(vac . vac);\n      {d, k, lam, obD[k, th, 2], If[OddQ[k], obD[k, th, 2] lam, lam/obD[k, th, 2]], z[[If[OddQ[k], 1, 4]]], Max[Abs[y - lam vac]]}, {k, 1, 4}]], {d, {1., 0.1, 0.001, 0.00001}}];\nobVacGrid = Grid[Prepend[Flatten[obVacTest, 1], {\"theta_A - theta_F\", \"k\", \"tau(theta_k) on vac\", \"d_k\", \"hat tau_k\", \"z_1 or z_4\", \"|vac t - tau vac|\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left];\nobSetup[3];  (* restore the L = 3 index tables for any later re-run *)\nobVacGrid",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
