  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**[numpy cross-check of the cell above; the Wolfram cell was NOT run, see the status note at the end]** Twisted vacuum, L = 2, theta = (0.3, 0.3 − d, 0.3, 0.3 − d), z = (1.3, 0.8, 1.1, 0.7) (the vacuum bra is an exact eigenbra, residual 0 to machine precision): tau(theta_k) -> 0 like d^2 for every k, d_k -> infinity (k odd) / 0 (k even) like d^-2 / d^2, and the normalised eigenvalues stay exactly z_1 (k odd) and z_4 (k even):\n\n| d = theta_A - theta_F | tau(theta_1) | d_1 | hat tau_1 | tau(theta_2) | d_2 | hat tau_2 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 (ABJM point 2h) | 0.325 | 4 | 1.3 | 0.175 | 0.25 | 0.7 |\n| 0.1 | 3.25e-3 | 400 | 1.3 | 1.75e-3 | 2.5e-3 | 0.7 |\n| 1e-3 | 3.25e-7 | 4e6 | 1.3 | 1.75e-7 | 2.5e-7 | 0.7 |\n| 1e-5 | 3.25e-11 | 4e10 | 1.3 | 1.75e-11 | 2.5e-11 | 0.7 |\n\n(k = 3, 4 repeat k = 1, 2 since theta_3 = theta_1, theta_4 = theta_2.) So the normalisation hat t_k = d_k^(+-1) t1(theta_k) removes exactly the singularity of the theta_A = theta_F limit, as 2603's hat t does.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary (2026-10-12) and status of this notebook\n\n**Status / what ran where.** Cells 1-14 (all of section 1 and the exact finite-twist word identities of section 2) were executed in the shared Wolfram kernel and carry native outputs. During the session the kernel died (machine out of memory, the VS Code extension host grew to 14-19 GB) and could not be restarted: `wolfram.exe` prints *\"Wolfram Language 15.0.0 Engine license you are using has expired ... No valid password found\"* (`%APPDATA%\\WolframEngine\\Licensing\\mathpass`). Cells 16-34 (HW data, twisted eigenvectors, untwisting tables, mixed placements, homogeneous limit) are therefore written but NOT yet run; the code is a line-by-line transliteration of the numpy implementation (`scratchpad/oddbridge/{ob,hw,untw}.py`; python used only because the wolfbook kernel was blocked, as the repo rule allows), and the numpy results are pasted into the markdown cell under each unrun cell. Rerun cells 16-34 (expected 2-4 minutes) once the licence is renewed and compare with those tables.\n\n**1. Closed forms, all L [exact at L = 2, 3 (three parameter sets, h = 1/2 and h = 3/7, W_a and a generic BPS pair); machine precision at L = 4; symbolic identities for L = 1..4].** With the reference (v (x) u)^L, v.u = 0, P_k = reference with the first k sites rotated by the torus (Lambda^-1 on A, Lambda on F), theta_ks = theta_k - theta_s:\n- k odd (A, inverse letter): 1/d_k = h prod_{s != k} vartheta_ks, vartheta_ks = theta_ks (s F), theta_ks + h (s A); P_{k-1} t1(theta_k)^-1 = d_k P_k.\n- k even (F, forward letter): d_k = -h prod_{s != k} vartheta~_ks, vartheta~_ks = theta_ks (s A), theta_ks - h (s F); P_{k-1} t1(theta_k) = d_k P_k.\n- c_k = d_1 ... d_k: c_1 = 1/(h prod_F theta_1s prod_{A, s != 1} (theta_1s + h)) (the 5.5 formula, now proved); **c_12 = c_2 = prod_{A, s >= 3} theta_2s/(theta_1s + h) prod_{F, s >= 4} (theta_2s - h)/theta_1s** (L = 2: theta_23 (theta_24 - h)/((theta_13 + h) theta_14)); the whole chain (global torus) c_2L = prod_{F < F'} (h^2 - theta_FF'^2)/prod_{A < A'} (h^2 - theta_AA'^2) (L = 2: c_4 = (h^2 - theta_24^2)/(h^2 - theta_13^2) = -1108723/174000, and c_3 = -321399232/112262625 reproduced). L = 3 tables of d_k, c_k (exact) in sections 1b and 3.\n- Proof: one-site contraction lemma (A/F Lax contracted with an aux row/column is a scalar when the vectors are BPS-orthogonal or coincide), t1(theta_k) = h sum e_ij [M_> Lambda M_<]_ji (A) resp. -h sum e_ba [..]_ba (F); the singlet terms vanish because the torus preserves v.u = 0; needs identical (v, u) on all pairs.\n\n**2. One-field families at L = 3 [exact word identities for all six k; numpy for the twisted/untwisting tables].** F family: bra = reference . t1(th_1)^-1 t1(th_2) ... t1(th_{k-1})^-1 (alpha + beta t1(th_k)), alpha = (c eps - 1)/c_{k-1}, beta = 1/c_k puts u(c eps - 1 + Lambda) on the F site of pair p = k/2; A family (alpha = 1/c_{k-1}, beta = -kappa/c_k, kappa = 1 - c eps, letter t1(th_k)^-1) puts v(1 - kappa Lambda^-1). Limit = V0 + (a - a') C_1 resp. V0 + (a'' - a) C_1, a' = a(c + phi_1)/(c + phi_4), a'' = a(c + phi_4)/(c + phi_1). Non-zero for exactly four saved states: the vacuum [3,0,3] (V0 = 1) and the three [2,0,2] states (weight (L-1)(e1 - e4); E_MZ = 8, 8, 16) with X11 = X44 = C_1(data) = +i/sqrt(24), -i/sqrt(24), 1/sqrt(24) (C_3 = C_5 = C_1 as well). Convergence O(eps) (rate 0.99-1.00), phi- and c-independent (X_est = C_1 to 7.4e-5 at eps = 1e-4 for three (phi, c)), finite-twist identity 5e-15, B_1 control (a = -1, kappa = z_4): z_1 T_eps = <B_1|Psi_eps> to 1e-13. The other 22 states give T -> 0.\n\n**3. Mixed placements [exact words; numpy limits].** k = 3, 4 (pair 2) and k = 5, 6 (pair 3): same site rotation matrices, constants through c_{k-1}, c_k; limits equal the pair-1 ones (cyclicity: X_p = C_1 for all p, |psi - S psi| <= 7e-16); finite-eps differences O(eps). The A family on pair 2, t1(th_1)^-1 t1(th_2) (alpha + beta t1(th_3)^-1), localises exactly.\n\n**4. Homogeneous limit.** At the ABJM point nothing is singular as delta -> 0 (c_1 = (2 h^2)^(-L) = 8 at L = 3, d_2 = 1/8, c_12 = 1): T_eps(delta) is smooth, with a regular value at delta = 0 exactly. The singular locus is theta_A = theta_F: d_k ~ (theta_A - theta_F)^(-L) for k odd and ~ (theta_A - theta_F)^(+L) for k even, tau(theta_k) ~ (theta_A - theta_F)^L, hat tau_k = z_1 or z_4 exactly on the vacuum. Normalised letters hat t_k = d_k t1(theta_k) (k odd), t1(theta_k)/d_k (k even): overlap = [prod_{j<k} hat tau_j^((-1)^j)] (c eps - 1 + hat tau_k) <W_a^L|Psi_eps> (F), and V0 + (a - a') C_1 = lim (c eps - 1 + hat tau_2)/(hat tau_1 eps (c + phi_4)) <W_a^L|Psi_eps> (pair 1). For the [2,0,2] states hat tau_1 = hat tau_2 -> i, -i, -1 and C_1 = (1 - 1/hat tau_1) K, K = lim <W_a^L|Psi_eps>/(eps a (phi_4 - phi_1)) = (1 + i)/sqrt(96), (1 - i)/sqrt(96), 1/sqrt(96) (phi-, a-, c-independent; tested at delta = 0).\n\n**Not done / open.** Even bridges (a pair) are still not reached: the A-site and F-site families are the only free one-site rotations available on the non-good reference. The relation hat tau_1 = hat tau_2 = fourth roots of unity at the odd-bridge states (and K as a Slater determinant of Q-functions) is observed numerically, not derived.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Rerun 2026-10-13 (Wolfram licence renewed)\n\nCells 3, 5, 7, 14 (definitions and exact checks) and all previously unrun cells 16, 19, 22, 25, 27, 30, 32, 34 were run in the live kernel and now carry native outputs; cells 8, 10, 12 keep their outputs from the original session (not rerun: 12 is the 44 s machine-precision L = 4 check). **Every numpy number quoted under the cells was reproduced** (cells 19-34 take 75 s in total, cell 19 alone 15 s): \n- 2b (cell 19): pair-1 F/A families, error to the limit 8.92e-3 / 8.99e-4 / 9.00e-5 (vacuum), 4.62e-3 / 4.65e-4 / 4.66e-5 (E = 8, F), 3.38e-3 / 3.40e-4 / 3.40e-5 (E = 16, F), 1.47e-3 / 1.48e-4 / 1.48e-5 and 9.95e-4 / 1.00e-4 / 1.00e-5 (A); finite-twist identity residual below the print threshold 1e-13 (python: <= 5.6e-15).\n- 2c (cell 22): X_est - C_1 = 6.3e-5 / 4.6e-5 (phi1, c = 2, F), 6.4e-5 / 4.4e-5 (A), 7.4e-5 / 5.7e-5 (phi2), 4.1e-5 / 3.1e-5 (c = 0.5); convergence rates 0.996 / 1.000 etc.; B_1 control difference <= 1.1e-13.\n- 3 (cell 25): all six placements, e.g. k = 3: 2.90e-4 (vacuum), 1.12e-5 (E = 8), 2.82e-6 (E = 16); k = 6: 4.90e-4, 7.99e-5, 8.02e-5.\n- 3 (cell 27): exact d_k, c_k as in the table (769088320/14100753, ..., c_6 = 6333341157664592071/1358814566556000000).\n- 4 (cells 30, 32, 34): the delta-scan (c_1 = 6.3745 ... 8, d_2 = 0.13798 ... 1/8, T_eps = -0.024883-0.14549i ... -9.32e-5-0.15092i), hat tau_1 = hat tau_2 -> +i, -i, -1 with K = (1+i)/sqrt(96) etc., and the vacuum / theta_A -> theta_F table.\n\n(fixed 2026-10-13: cell 16 imported the whole `abjm-hw-states.wxf` (its L4 key is 3 GB in memory); it now reads `checks/session-2026-10-13/epsexp/hw_L3.json` with `Import[..., \"RawJSON\"]`, same 26 states in the same order. No other port bug found. The 'NOT run' labels in the markdown cells under the cells are historical.)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
